# Vendored Remotion Skills

This template ships two Claude Code skills, both auto-loaded on `git clone` (no install command).

## `.claude/skills/remotion/` (vendored)
Mirrored from [remotion-dev/skills](https://github.com/remotion-dev/skills) `skills/remotion/` subtree. Contains:
- `SKILL.md` — main "remotion-best-practices" entry
- `rules/*.md` — 35 reference docs covering transitions, captions, audio, Tailwind, fonts, FFmpeg, light leaks, etc.
- `rules/assets/` — supporting binary assets

The vendored upstream commit SHA is recorded in `.claude/skills/remotion/SOURCE.md`.

## `.claude/skills/remotion-docker-template/SKILL.md` (project-specific)
Hand-written guidance for THIS template — composition map, atomic-design layout, Docker workflow, Tailwind rules, Lambda commands. Edit this file when project conventions change.

## Refreshing from upstream
```bash
npm run skills:sync
# or:
./scripts/sync-remotion-skills.sh
```

The script clones `remotion-dev/skills`, replaces `.claude/skills/remotion/` with the latest `skills/remotion/` subtree, and updates `SOURCE.md` with the new SHA.

## When to consult which skill
- Remotion API patterns (transitions, captions, audio, FFmpeg, fonts) → `remotion-best-practices` (vendored)
- This template's compositions, Docker pipeline, Tailwind setup → `remotion-docker-template`
